# Canonical author identity for git's history output.
#
# Commits made locally carry `Carlos Ortiz <orgoca@gmail.com>`; pull requests
# merged through the GitHub web interface record the account's noreply
# address instead. Both are the same person, and without this file
# `git shortlog`, `git log` and `git blame` present a single-author project
# as having two contributors — the wrong impression for anyone checking
# authorship from a clone.
#
# The committer on web merges stays `GitHub <noreply@github.com>`, because
# that is what actually created those merge commits. Only the author is
# canonicalised here, and no commit is rewritten; this changes what git
# displays, not what it stores. GitHub's own contributor graph does not read
# this file.

Carlos Ortiz <orgoca@gmail.com> <35277730+orgoca@users.noreply.github.com>
Carlos Ortiz <orgoca@gmail.com> orgoca <35277730+orgoca@users.noreply.github.com>
